## Summary

**Deliverable:** `/work/submission.csv` — 240 rows, columns `[battle_turn, pikachu_hp]`, IDs identical to `/data/sample_submission.csv` in the same order, no missing values, HP predictions rounded to integers in [1, 78].

**Approach**
- **Data structure:** 3334 battles (rounds) × 24 turns; test = rounds 1828–1837, which are *different* battles from train despite overlapping round numbers (zero feature/battle_turn overlap). All test categorical values exist in train.
- **Baseline:** HP mechanic `clip(previous_hp − damage_dealt + healing_applied, 0, max_hp)` → validation R2 ≈ 0.40.
- **Model:** LightGBM regression with native categorical features (10 categorical columns, NaN handled natively) + engineered features (mechanic HP, prev/max ratio, damage/prev, KO flag, turn/round, damage × type effectiveness).
- **Validation:** round-wise (grouped) split — rounds ≤ 2668 train (64k rows) / > 2668 validation (16k rows) — to prevent serial HP leakage across turns of the same battle.
- **Tuning:** 40 optuna trials → best validation **R2 = 0.970** (params logged in `/work/harness-state/evidence.md`).
- **Final:** trained on all 80,016 rows, clipped to [0, max_hp], rounded.

**Verification (all PASS)**
- Columns and ID order match `sample_submission.csv` exactly (pandas diff)
- 240 rows, no NaNs, all finite

**Note:** harness state files live under `/work/harness-state/` (`intent.md`, `evidence.md`, `aar.md`, `train_model.py`) because `/work/.harness` is owned by uid 1001 and not writable by this agent (uid 1000).

**Residual assumption:** test labels follow the same distribution as train (unverifiable without test targets); if the hidden test R2 is far below 0.97, distribution shift in the damage/stage mechanics would be the likely cause.
